Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"8e78b00a-640d-a142-829d-a0e304ead379"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7465ac89-6b75-7845-b6e9-76531f8c3515"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"aef9e37e-e43d-0a4f-8694-7a064ef9e485"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"178510ed-a76c-a540-a234-e74151fa3970"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4bf37c3d-2d0b-1e4e-9888-4481a7fa7f95"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7b8cd36a-146f-8749-9dc2-0119d7e0d480"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d419f396-6d5c-d54f-adf9-c32ba8156fd3"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0129e065-c6da-ce44-a6f8-12449ad48cd4"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"06f5287a-7faa-a743-a413-6820b0ab0428"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ce63d18b-d56f-c74b-9dff-da9939a10c0f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"0a41b3f6-4333-ab4d-be51-1d760ba91313"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"c733d632-7f55-1a48-9832-fd3c1e6e3c5f"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"030af61f-7916-9349-8c15-50a39534be24"],

